{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (via the cobbler-scaffold orchestrator) requested implementation of Task #5230: `[stitch] cmd/pwd: features implementation (srd051-pwd R1.1-R1.4)`. This is a code generation task to create `cmd/pwd/main.go` - a Go reimplementation of the GNU `pwd` utility that prints the current working directory. The implementation must support logical (-L/--logical) and physical (-P/--physical) modes, match GNU `gpwd` behavior byte-for-byte, and follow the project's execution constitution and Go style guidelines. Git is managed externally; only code writing and verification is expected.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU coreutils `pwd` utility reimplementation in Go\n   - Logical mode (-L): uses PWD environment variable, preserving symlink names\n   - Physical mode (-P): resolves all symlinks via filesystem (this is the DEFAULT)\n   - Last-flag-wins precedence when both -L and -P are specified\n   - SIGPIPE handler installation via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Differential testing against `gpwd` Homebrew reference binary\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` for test verification\n   - PWD validation: must name current directory and contain no `.` or `..` components\n   - Error handling: positional operands and unknown flags produce stderr errors with exit 1\n   - Copyright header: `// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.` + `// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT`\n   - Function size hard limit: 40 lines\n   - File size limit: 500 lines\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd051-pwd.yaml` (READ)\n     - This is the SRD defining all requirements for the pwd utility\n     - Critical for understanding the exact behavior to implement\n     - Key requirements:\n       - R1.1: Default prints CWD + newline, exit 0, default mode is **-P (physical)**\n       - R1.2: `-L` (--logical) prints PWD env var if valid (names current dir, no `.`/`..` components); falls back to physical if PWD unset/invalid\n       - R1.3: `-P` (--physical) resolves all symlinks\n       - R1.4: When both -L and -P given, last one wins\n       - R2.1: Positional operands → stderr error, exit 1\n       - R2.2: Unknown flags → stderr error, exit 1\n       - R3.1-R3.3: Differential testing with LC_ALL=C\n     - Non-goals: no directory changing, no output formatting options\n   \n   - `cmd/pwd/main.go` (TO BE CREATED)\n     - The main implementation file for the pwd utility\n     - Must follow patterns from existing cmd/ packages (SIGPIPE handler, copyright header)\n   \n   - `pkg/sys/sigpipe.go` (PROVIDED in project_context)\n     - Contains `InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` that must be called at start of main()\n     - Pattern: `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` as first call in main()\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Implementation has not started.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand full requirements before implementation\n   - No implementation or debugging has occurred yet\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: Extremely detailed task specification including role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, source code, requirement states), execution constitution, Go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is to implement `cmd/pwd/main.go` following srd051-pwd R1.1-R1.4.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/pwd/main.go` implementing srd051-pwd R1.1 through R1.4\n   - Verify compilation: `go build -o bin/pwd ./cmd/pwd/`\n   - Verify no vet issues: `go vet ./cmd/pwd/...`\n   - Run the binary to confirm it prints CWD and exits 0\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd051-pwd.yaml`) and was about to begin implementing `cmd/pwd/main.go`. The SRD read was the first step in the task's prescribed workflow: \"Review provided context\" → \"Plan approach\" → \"Implement\" → \"Verify\". I completed step 1 (review) and was about to proceed to step 2 (plan) and step 3 (implement).\n\n   The implementation needs to:\n   - Start with SPDX copyright header\n   - Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first in main()\n   - Parse `-L`/`--logical` and `-P`/`--physical` flags (last one wins)\n   - Default to physical mode (-P) when no flags given\n   - In logical mode: check PWD env var validity (names current dir, no `.`/`..`), fall back to physical if invalid\n   - In physical mode: use something like `filepath.EvalSymlinks` + `os.Getwd()`\n   - Reject positional operands with stderr error and exit 1\n   - Reject unknown flags with stderr error and exit 1\n   - Print result to stdout with trailing newline, exit 0\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write `cmd/pwd/main.go` implementing all R1.1-R1.4 requirements from srd051-pwd, then verify with `go build -o bin/pwd ./cmd/pwd/` and `go vet ./cmd/pwd/...`. The task description states: \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.1 as specified in the SRD -- core default behavior\", \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.2 -- logical mode\", \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.3 -- physical mode\", \"Implement srd051-pwd R1.4 -- flag parsing, mode selection\". Design decision D1: \"Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main()\". Design decision D3: \"Parse flags using the standard library flag package or os.Args manual parsing as dictated by the SRD -- GNU pwd uses long options (--logical, --physical)\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, o