{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015uG6mrx6QbiadECRENgQ97","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"There are two issues:\n\n1. **Logical mode (`-L`)**: Both our binary and `gpwd` output the symlink path, but our binary outputs `/var/folders/...` while gpwd outputs `/var/folders/...` too. They match! Good.\n\n2. **Physical mode (`-P`)**: Our binary outputs the symlink path `/var/folders/.../link` instead of the resolved path `/private/var/folders/.../real`. The reference binary outputs `/private/var/folders/.../real`.\n\nSo there are two problems:\n- Physical mode is not resolving the symlink. `os.Getwd()` on macOS returns a path through `/var` which is itself a symlink to `/private/var`. \n\nThe core issue is that `os.Getwd()` returns the path as accessed through symlinks rather than resolving them to their physical locations, so I need to implement actual symlink resolution for the `-P` flag. I'm realizing the core issue: on macOS, when you `cd` into a symlinked directory, the kernel's `getcwd()` returns the path as you navigated to it (through the symlink), not the fully resolved physical path. So even though `/var` is a symlink to `/private/var`, if you `cd /var/folders/...`, `getcwd()` returns that `/var/...` path rather than resolving it to `/private/var/...`. That's why I need `filepath.EvalSymlinks` to get the actual physical path that matches what `pwd -P` would show.\n\nThe logical mode is already working correctly—it's preserving the symlink path from the PWD environment variable, which matches what GNU `pwd -L` does.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":35318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":481},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78aabc7d-55d4-4690-a9a1-d1597569ac6c","uuid":"2f571c9c-107a-4101-8a1a-8ea11db2508b"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_015uG6mrx6QbiadECRENgQ97","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Physical mode isn't resolving symlinks fully. `os.Getwd()` doesn't resolve `/var` → `/private/var` or user symlinks on macOS. I need to use `filepath.EvalSymlinks`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":481,"cache_read_input_tokens":35318,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":481},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"78aabc7d-55d4-4690-a9a1-d1597569ac6c","uuid":"c231044e-40e9-4420-be86-34b415e8c238"}
